# Accepted risks for `trivy config` (report-only scan in CI). Each entry has a reason.
# Revisit before using this setup for anything beyond a course demo.

# EKS API endpoint is reachable from the internet (CRITICAL x2).
# Needed so kubectl/Helm on a laptop and CI can reach the cluster without a VPN or bastion host.
# Access still requires AWS IAM authentication. Production fix: endpoint_public_access_cidrs or private-only.
AWS-0040
AWS-0041

# Worker node security group allows all outbound traffic (CRITICAL).
# Nodes must pull images from GHCR/ECR and reach AWS APIs; egress goes through the NAT gateway.
AWS-0104

# No EKS control-plane logging to CloudWatch (MEDIUM). Billed per GB; observability comes from
# Prometheus/Grafana in-cluster instead.
AWS-0038

# No VPC flow logs (MEDIUM). Billed per GB; not needed for a short-lived demo environment.
AWS-0178
